         I searched the linux-ide mailing list and lkml, and i am 
surprised such a big problem was not reported. I'm sorry if i am 
sending this to the wrong list.

         My southbridge is VT8237. I tried this with APIC enabled and 
disabled, it still doesn't work.

         hda is ST325082 (250GB Seagate Barracuda 7200.8)
         hdb is Philips CDD5301 Combo DVD/CD

         hdc is Maxtor 6 L040J2 (40GB; all versions of Linux work if 
this is hda instead of hdc)
         hdd is TEAC CD-540E (CD drive)

         I also have a harddisk on SATA (with my Linux partition on 
it). I use libata to access it, but i don't use libata for anything else.

         Just as Linux boots, it prints out
hda:irq probe failed
         and then a lot of messages scroll by. There is a stack 
trace, but i can't the the beginning of it. The first element in the 
stack trace that i can see is

[something] request_irq+0x8a/0xc0

         After the stack trace:
handlers: ide_intr
Disabling IRQ #14
(other messages about hdc, hdd, etc.)

         At this point the kernel seems to freeze, and i can't use 
pageup to see earlier messages. SysRq doesn't work either.

         I attached my .config.

         I have a single processor, 1GHz Athlon, A7V600-X motherboard 
with KT600 northbridge.
         My kernel command line is root=/dev/sda5 ro reboot=w 
floppy=daring atkbd.softraw=0.

